<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Nexauren Hub" description="Read how Nexauren Hub handles browser-side file processing, website requests and privacy-related choices.">
<main id="main-content" class="page-main"><div class="container narrow-container"><nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy</span></nav><header class="page-hero compact-hero"><span class="eyebrow">LEGAL · PRIVACY</span><h1>Privacy <span class="gradient-text">policy.</span></h1><p>Last updated: 20 October 2026. This starter policy describes the current tool-only version and should be reviewed before commercial launch.</p></header>
<article class="content-prose long-form"><h2>1. Scope</h2><p>Nexauren Hub provides online tools for images, PDF documents, text and audio. This policy covers the current website. If accounts, analytics, storage or payments are introduced, the policy must be updated before those features launch.</p><h2>2. Files and tool processing</h2><p>Image tools use browser graphics APIs, PDF tasks use pdf-lib in the browser, text tasks operate on text in the current page, and audio tools use browser audio decoding. These tools are designed to process your selected content on your device instead of uploading it to a Nexauren processing server. Temporary data may remain in browser memory while a task runs.</p><h2>3. Website and hosting data</h2><p>Hosting and content-delivery infrastructure may receive technical request information such as IP address, requested path, browser/user-agent details, timing and errors for delivery or security. Exact logs, retention and provider responsibilities depend on the production configuration and must be confirmed before launch.</p><h2>4. Accounts, contact and payments</h2><p>Account, login, registration, dashboard and upgrade pages are interface previews only. They do not submit credentials, create accounts or process payments. A support email is shown only when configured. Do not enter real passwords into preview forms.</p><h2>5. Cookies and analytics</h2><p>The current frontend does not intentionally set advertising or analytics cookies. Hosting settings or future integrations can change this. Verify production behavior and update the cookie information and consent flow if non-essential storage is introduced.</p><h2>6. Sensitive content</h2><p>Only process content you are authorized to use. Browser-side file processing does not prevent ordinary network requests for website assets or hosting logs.</p><h2>7. Your choices</h2><p>You can choose not to use a tool, close the page and keep downloaded files under your own control. Contact details should be provided by the site operator when the official address has been configured.</p><h2>8. Changes and contact</h2><p>This policy may change as the product evolves. Before publication, the responsible legal entity should add an appropriate contact address, verified hosting practices, retention details and rights information required in the markets served. This starter text is not legal advice.</p></article></div></main>
</BaseLayout>